# clang-tools-extra — lift-source

THERE IS NO clang-tools-extra-feedstock. Verified: `gh api
repos/conda-forge/clang-tools-extra-feedstock` 404s, and a repo search across
the conda-forge org for `clang` returns no such repo.

It lives INSIDE clangdev-feedstock: a `clang-tools-extra/*` source entry
feeding that recipe's `clang-tools` output (alongside clang-format,
clang-scan-deps and the rest).

Upstream: https://github.com/conda-forge/clangdev-feedstock
Fork:     https://github.com/NAGAGroup/clangdev-feedstock
Pinned:   28ab51758156090b64f141cb7080164e57dbed08 (conda-forge main, 2026-08-29)

So the PINNED_REF here is deliberately the same commit as ../clangdev — one
fork, two lifts. What we take is the clang-tools-extra source wiring and the
output carve, which feeds our acpp-tools output.
